        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The major bearing surfaces of the lathe bed have now been completed and we can turn our attention to the rear carriage gib way of the bed, shown as (5) in Fig. 26.34. This surface is used as a hold-down bearing surface for the carriage and is situated directly under the rear inverted V-way of the bed. On some lathes the rear carriage gib way of the bed is in direct bearing contact with the gib bracket (7) boiled to the rear carriage gib bracket bearing represented by (6) in Fig. 26.39. This clamping strip (gib",
